From 2c22014d8cb7b658d8384f3e31dfdda54d82699a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:56:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(approval): a grant written in chat clears smart approval
 for that source

Jacob wrote in a chat "It is approved for agents and subagents to run code in clones of github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent", yet a subagent's pytest in such a clone stayed on a card. 0084 reads the root chat live, but only the session store and the root agent's flushed list: a message typed while the root agent waits on a subagent sits in the root agent's steer buffer (or the queued admissions) and reached neither, so the judge never saw the grant. The held card was also never reviewed again when the user wrote, and a grant dropped out of the review once compaction removed its message.

A user message of the chat, or of its root chat for a subagent at any depth, that lets agents run code from a named repository now covers later commands that run code in a clone of exactly that repository (host and owner/repo), until the user withdraws it in the chat. The review reads the user's waiting messages too, and each User line carries its time. A held card is re-reviewed when the user writes and settles as allowed once when the new words clear it. New card choice `source` ("Always allow code from this source in this chat") records a grant. Grants are kept with the chat in the session store (state_meta approval_grants:<session>), never in config. Peer-agent messages, subagent results, parent goals and steers, tool output and files never grant; another repo, a fork name or a look-alike host is not covered. No new key.
